>You, by contrast, are assuming that one particular playing style - your
>own, I can only presume - is, absolutely and undeniably, best.

"Playing style" is used as a cover for all kinds of sillyness. Of course
there _is_ an objectively best (highest odds of ascension) move in each
situation. We don't always know what it is, but in many cases we can. For
example, if you aren't standing near water it is best to be wearing a
cloak that provides a benefit in that situation. If you see a monster that
could be a were-creature, it is best to check if it is a were-creature. 

There's room for genuine disagreements about what is best. That doesn't
mean that doing something daft because of "playing style" makes it any
less daft.
